## 34) Final Revision Points
- SQL is declarative: you define what to fetch, not step-by-step how.
- Good schema design is as important as writing good queries.
- Indexes improve reads, but too many indexes hurt writes.
- Joins and aggregations are core for real-world tasks.
- Transactions protect consistency in multi-step updates.
- Always test with realistic data volume.

